commit 12d86ceba772ef055085dafd9f7bfb64594f756f
Author: LinLinHua <lhua@modular.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 29 14:30:46 2026 -0700

    [KB] Nemotron-H FP8 bring-up + autonomous in-place SSM decode
    optimization
    
    Brings up `nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Nano-4B-FP8` (Nemotron-H: a 42-layer
    hybrid Mamba-2 + NoPE GQA-attention + relu2-MLP decoder, modelopt
    per-tensor FP8) in MAX, and lands a verified decode optimization.
    
    - New kernel `mamba2_ssd_chunk_scan_varlen_fwd` (Mamba-2 SSD
    chunked-scan, parity vs HuggingFace ~1e-16), registered in the builtin
    kernel library; it also serves decode (the existing state-update op caps
    at `dstate` 16; Nemotron-H uses 128).
    - New `nemotron_h` pipeline architecture (config, modules, weight
    adapters, hybrid paged-KV + slot-indexed SSM/conv state cache).
    Random-weight logit-verify vs HuggingFace: cosine 0.9999.
    - Decode optimization — in-place SSM state-pool write-back: profiling
    found ~35% of decode GPU time was a whole-pool read-modify-write every
    step (near the HBM roofline, but only the active slots change); the
    in-place variant writes just those slots.
    
    Result on B200 (matched-completion sweep), baseline → optimized:
    
    | concurrency | output tok/s | TPOT mean (ms) |
    |---|---|---|
    | 16 | 876 → 1432 (+63.5%) | 16.1 → 10.0 |
    | 32 | 926 → 1408 (+52.0%) | 24.8 → 16.2 |
    
    gsm8k held (strict-match 70%). Full results + profile + validation
    detail: `utils/kb/nemotron-3-nano-4b-fp8-opt-loop-results.md`.
    MODULAR_ORIG_COMMIT_REV_ID: 5fedbdfc5452e7b2e534170e3b255ba7c21dc86b

