    Both methods are designed to be invoked from a containing parent
    Module's ``forward`` so they land in one traced graph and bind the
    BN parameters exactly once.
    
    The ``flux_modulev3`` package is self-contained: encoder, decoder,
    their building blocks (Down/Up/Mid blocks, Downsample/Upsample/
    Resnet/VAEAttention layers), and the ``AutoencoderKLFlux2`` config
    class all live alongside the ``Vae`` Module with no imports from
    ``autoencoders_modulev3``.
    
    Includes 13 unit tests covering construction, the dual entry-point
    contract (``forward`` raises), ``input_types`` declaration, shared
    BN topology (``bn_mean`` / ``bn_var`` live only on the ``Vae``
    root and are never duplicated under ``encoder`` / ``decoder``),
    the full ``adapt_state_dict`` key map (encoder, decoder,
    quant_conv, post_quant_conv, bn), eager encode shape, and a
    headline parameter-sharing assertion through a small wrapper
    Module that mirrors how the production FLUX.2 parent embeds
    the ``Vae``.
    
    Also extends the default ``Module.forward`` ``NotImplementedError``
    message to point readers at the multi-entry-point alternative, so
    Modules using the dual-method pattern (like ``Vae``) don't need a
    custom stub purely to produce a clear error.
    
